	        No Obsidian yet? <a href={COMMUNITY_URL}>View in the community catalogue</a>
	      </span>
	    </p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="graph-cap"><span class="lm">●</span> a sample vault, sorting itself into topics</div>
	</header>

	<section id="demo">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
	      <h2>Connect your notes, then build on them</h2>
	      <p>
	        One evening of exam prep — the map connects what you wrote, the agent
	        builds on a topic, and search by meaning pulls in the note you forgot
	        you had.
	      </p>
	    </div>

	    {/* A mock of the real workspace: file list, smart graph pane, chat pane,
	        with the search modal floating over it — the same three views the
	        plugin adds to Obsidian. The storyline is driven by landing.js. */}
	    <div class="vault" id="vault">
	      <div class="vault-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>My vault — Obsidian</span></div>
	      {/* data-pane drives the mobile one-pane-at-a-time view; the storyline
	          moves it graph → chat → graph. Ignored on desktop. */}
	      <div class="vault-body" data-pane="graph">
	        <div class="v-main">
	          <div class="v-graph">
	            <canvas id="miniGraph" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
	            {/* Simulated cursor — shown only for the graph's direct
	                manipulations (lassoing, pressing the bar buttons), where
	                seeing the hand is what makes them read as gestures. */}
	            <span class="v-cursor" id="vCursor" aria-hidden="true">
	              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 2.5 19 12.2l-6.1.7-3.2 5.6z"/></svg>
	            </span>
	            {/* Selection and exit bars live inside the graph pane so they
	                centre on the graph, not on the whole window. */}
	            <div class="v-selbar" id="vSel" aria-hidden="true">
	              <strong>24</strong> notes selected
	              <span class="v-selact" id="vImm">Immerse</span>
	              <span class="v-selact">Collapse</span>
	            </div>
	            {/* Second selection, inside the immersion: a sub-topic lassoed
	                and handed to the chat — the real bar's "Open in Chat". */}
	            <div class="v-selbar" id="vSel2" aria-hidden="true">
	              <strong>9</strong> notes selected
	              <span class="v-selact" id="vOpen">Open in chat</span>
	            </div>
	            {/* Shown while immersed — the way back out of the topic. */}
	            <div class="v-selbar v-exitbar" id="vExit" aria-hidden="true">
	              Immersed in <strong>Memory</strong>
	              <span class="v-selact" id="vExitBtn">Exit</span>
	            </div>
	          </div>
	        </div>

	        <aside class="v-chat">
	          <div class="v-chat-body" id="vChat"></div>
	          <div class="v-composer">
	            {/* Context chips: the ambient graph selection (immersed topic)
	                and, later, a note attached from search (⌥A) — the same
	                shapes the real composer uses. */}
	            <div class="v-attach" id="vAttach" aria-hidden="true">
	              <span class="v-att-chip v-att-graph" id="vGchip" hidden>◉ 9 graph notes</span>
	              <span class="v-att-chip" id="vLchip" hidden>Lecture 8 — Sleep.md</span>
	            </div>
	            {/* Questions are typed here, in the composer — not in the search
	                modal, which is for finding notes. */}
	            <div class="v-comp-input">
	              <span id="vcTyped"></span><span class="v-caret" id="vcCaret" hidden></span>
	              <span class="v-comp-ph" id="vcPh">Type a message…</span>
	            </div>
	            <div class="v-comp-row">
	              <span class="v-plus">+</span>
	              <span class="v-agent">S2B Agent</span>
	              {/* Deliberately generic — naming a provider here would read as
	                  an endorsement, and the point is that you pick your own. */}
	              <span class="v-model">Your model</span>
	              <span class="v-send" id="vSend" aria-hidden="true">
	                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 19V5M5 12l7-7 7 7"/></svg>
	              </span>
	            </div>
	          </div>
	        </aside>

	        <div class="v-search" id="vSearch">
	          <div class="vs-box">
	            <div class="vs-input">
	              {/* Lucide `search`, matching the real modal: circle upper-left,
	                  handle running down to the lower-right. */}
	              <svg class="vs-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
	                <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7"></circle>
	                <path d="m15 15 6 6"></path>
	              </svg>
	              <span id="vsTyped"></span><span class="vs-caret"></span>
	              <span class="vs-ph" id="vsPh">Search notes with #tag or /folder…</span>
	            </div>
	            <div class="vs-empty" id="vsEmpty">No notes contain those words.</div>
	            {/* Selection summary, as the real modal shows above the results. */}
	            <div class="vs-sum" id="vsSum" aria-hidden="true">1 selected: Lecture 8 — Sleep</div>
	            <div class="vs-results" id="vsResults"></div>
	            <div class="vs-hints">
	              <span>↵ Open note</span>
	              <span id="vsAtt" class="vs-att">⌥A Attach to chat</span>
	              <span id="vsSem" class="vs-sem">⇥ semantic: off</span>
	              <span>esc Close</span>
	            </div>
	          </div>
	        </div>
	      </div>
	    </div>

	    {/* Each card jumps the storyline to its phase — landing.js binds them. */}
	    <ol class="steps" id="steps">
	      <li data-step="1">
	        <button type="button">
	          <strong>It connects itself</strong>
	          <span>No folders, no tagging. Related notes find each other and group into topics, named for what they're about.</span>
	        </button>
	      </li>
	      <li data-step="2">
	        <button type="button">
	          <strong>Immerse into a topic</strong>
	          <span>Circle any cluster to dive in — and watch it break apart into the finer topics hiding inside.</span>
	        </button>
	      </li>
	      <li data-step="3">
	        <button type="button">
	          <strong>Build on it with the agent</strong>
	          <span>Circle a sub-topic and open it in the chat. The agent reads those notes and drafts — nothing is saved without your OK.</span>
	        </button>
	      </li>
	      <li data-step="4">
	        <button type="button">
	          <strong>Search what you meant</strong>
	          <span>Missing a piece? Search by meaning finds the note you forgot you had — attach it, and the agent folds it in.</span>
	        </button>
	      </li>
	    </ol>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section id="privacy" style="background:var(--bg-2); border-block:1px solid var(--border);">
	  <div class="wrap privacy-wrap">
	    <div>
	      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
	      <h2 style="text-align:left">Your notes stay yours</h2>
	      <p style="color:var(--text-2); font-size:16.5px; margin:12px 0 22px;">
	        Run the AI on your own computer and nothing ever leaves it. Use a cloud one and you decide, note by note, what it may see.
	      </p>
	      <div class="toggle-row">
	        <button class="tg on" data-mode="local">On my computer</button>
	        <button class="tg" data-mode="cloud">Cloud AI</button>
	      </div>
	      <ul class="privacy-list">
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Untrusted until you say so.</strong> Cloud AI starts blocked from every private note.</span></li>
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Private by default.</strong> Only notes you allow can be read or sent anywhere.</span></li>
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Nothing written without you.</strong> Every edit waits for your approval first.</span></li>
	      </ul>
	    </div>

	    <div class="flow">
	      <div class="machine">
	        <span class="machine-label">your computer</span>
	        <div class="node-row">
	          <div class="fnode"><strong>your notes</strong><span>1,284 of them</span></div>
	          <span class="arrow">→</span>
	          <div class="fnode"><strong>the plugin</strong><span>reads &amp; organizes</span></div>
	          <span class="arrow" id="arr2">→</span>
	          <div class="fnode" id="localModel"><strong>local AI</strong><span>runs right here</span></div>
	        </div>
	      </div>
	      <div class="cloud-zone">
	        <div class="barrier blocked" id="barrier">✕ nothing crosses this line</div>
	        <div class="cloud-node" id="cloudNode" style="opacity:.4">☁ cloud AI — idle</div>
	      </div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section style="background:var(--bg-2); border-block:1px solid var(--border);">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">And then some</div>
	      <h2>Built for daily use</h2>
	    </div>
	    <div class="fgrid">
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Memory</span><h4>It remembers you</h4><p>Opt in and the agent keeps its own notes on your preferences and projects — as real notes in your vault, yours to read and edit.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Skills</span><h4>Teach it new tricks</h4><p>It comes knowing how to explore your vault, edit notes and search the web. Teach it more by writing plain notes.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Connections</span><h4>Bring your other tools</h4><p>Hook up outside tools and sources (via MCP) when you want the agent to reach beyond your vault.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">History</span><h4>Chats are notes too</h4><p>Every conversation is saved in your vault. Rewrite a question and the old thread stays — nothing is lost.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Images &amp; PDFs</span><h4>Beyond plain text</h4><p>Share them in chat with an AI that can look at them — the plugin checks what each one supports.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Helpers</span><h4>Delegate the busywork</h4><p>Hand a focused job to a second agent with its own instructions, and keep your conversation on topic.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Parallel</span><h4>Many chats at once</h4><p>Run several conversations side by side — none of them blocks another.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">Always current</span><h4>Never goes stale</h4><p>Memory keeps track of where things live in your vault instead of copying them — so answers follow your latest edits.</p></div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section id="start">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">Providers</div>
	      <h2>Bring the AI you trust</h2>
	      <p>Six kinds of provider — two run entirely on your own computer. Switch per chat.</p>
	    </div>
	    <div class="provs">
	      <div class="prov">OpenAI</div>
	      <div class="prov">Anthropic</div>
	      <div class="prov">Ollama <em>local</em></div>
	      <div class="prov">oMLX <em>local</em></div>
	      <div class="prov">OpenRouter</div>
	      <div class="prov">OpenAI-compatible</div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section class="final" style="background:var(--bg-2); border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
